<p>The International Olympic Committee said this week that athletes seeking to compete in women’s Olympic events must meet biological female eligibility criteria and undergo a one-time genetic test under a new policy that begins with the 2028 Summer Games in Los Angeles. The decision sets the Olympic framework that national teams and organizers will now work under for women’s events ahead of the next Summer Games.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/lzb5qsEZOtRiJGGgorNhI-oWEhzic1hOH_sivEkU_prNNm2yq6P-LlqKTHFwWDJlcN2aFGCYkAHMg2QmhjTaEJZMozQpCfrGg57PaQSyWvO_f-uzSiknog32xsdwhGAnfcl2qoVGEktTmEjsXz4HyfqgJSKTjQ8d1PEWtUtuyn94ejSztmKrEFBPXJUj8rIEIL0o-LmExtJqiObqzb5mbx4yep-WZPXRHI8aushq' alt='Kirsty Coventry, president of the International Olympic Committee and a former Olympic swimmer from Zimbabwe.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Patchwork ends: The IOC is no longer leaving eligibility for Olympic women’s events to individual federations, ending a system that produced different standards across sports.</li><li>Leadership signal: The New York Times described the move as the most significant decision since Kirsty Coventry was elected last year, making it an early test of her presidency.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>NPR analysis: NPR reported that the decision leaves key questions unresolved beyond the headline rule, especially how genetic testing will work in practice and how the policy will be applied before the Los Angeles Games. (<a href='https://www.npr.org/2026/03/26/nx-s1-5762579/ioc-bans-trans-women-events-genetic-testing'>NPR</a>)</li><li>Newsweek analysis via AllSides: Coverage highlighted the announcement as one of the most consequential Olympic eligibility shifts in recent history because it will shape planning and participation decisions ahead of LA 2028. (<a href='https://www.allsides.com/news/2026-03-26-0700/sports-how-olympics-transgender-ban-will-impact-la-2028-games'>AllSides</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.allsides.com/news/2026-03-26-0700/sports-olympics-bans-transgender-women-female-category'>Olympics bans transgender women from female category</a> - allsides.com</li><li><a href='https://www.npr.org/2026/03/26/nx-s1-5762579/ioc-bans-trans-women-events-genetic-testing'>The Olympic committee bans trans athletes from women&#x27;s events, raising many questions</a> - npr.org</li><li><a href='https://www.cbsnews.com/news/transgender-women-athletes-banned-womens-olympic-events-ioc-policy/'>Transgender women athletes banned from women&#x27;s Olympic events</a> - cbsnews.com</li><li><a href='https://www.nytimes.com/2026/03/26/world/olympics/ioc-transgender-athletes-ban.html'>Olympic Committee Bars Transgender Athletes From Women’s Events</a> - nytimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.abs-cbn.com/sports/othersports/2026/3/27/olympic-women-s-sport-to-be-limited-to-biological-females-0830'>The International Olympic Committee announces that participation in women&#x27;s events will be limited to athletes classified as female based on biological criteria, with eligibility determined through a one-time genetic test starting from the 2028 Olympic Games. The policy replaces previous rules that allowed individual sports federations to set their own criteria.</a> - abs-cbn.com</li></ul>